### 5. AI Engine Optimization (Lightning Fast Moves)

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The current AI is extremely slow because it rebuilds the board state from FEN strings for every candidate move.
> **Action Plan:** We will completely overhaul [AIEngine](file:///d:/PP942920DRIVE/PROJECTS/chess/app/lib/domain/engine/ai_engine.dart#5-138) and [ChessEngine](file:///d:/PP942920DRIVE/PROJECTS/chess/app/lib/domain/engine/chess_engine.dart#103-766) to implement advanced search algorithms directly in Dart. This avoids complicated WebAssembly/JS interop issues with Stockfish on Cloudflare Pages, while delivering a chess engine that feels instantaneous on web. If required by the user, we can explore adding Stockfish.js as a Web Worker, but a highly optimized Dart Minimax will easily handle 5+ depths in under a second.

#### [MODIFY] [chess_engine.dart](file:///d:/PP942920DRIVE/PROJECTS/chess/app/lib/domain/engine/chess_engine.dart)
- Add hyper-fast [makeMove(Move)](file:///d:/PP942920DRIVE/PROJECTS/chess/app/lib/domain/engine/chess_engine.dart#187-198) and `unmakeMove(Move)` methods to eliminate the need for `ChessEngine.fromFEN()` during AI evaluation.
- Optimize legal move generation using bitboards or flat 1D arrays instead of 2D object arrays if necessary.

#### [MODIFY] [ai_engine.dart](file:///d:/PP942920DRIVE/PROJECTS/chess/app/lib/domain/engine/ai_engine.dart)
Implement the exact optimizations requested:
- **Minimax Algorithm:** Enhance the existing alpha-beta pruning with a transposition table.
- **Iterative Deepening:** Iterate through depths (1, 2, 3...) keeping time limits in check, rather than locking up the UI for a fixed depth. This guarantees moving instantly if the best move is obvious, and allows sorting moves using a principal variation.
- **Quiescence Search:** Continue searching capture sequences past the normal depth limit to avoid the horizon effect (blundering pieces immediately after the search cuts off).
- **Null Move Pruning & LMR (Late Move Reductions):** Advanced search heuristics to prune branches where doing nothing still leaves the player ahead, dramatically cutting down the search tree size.
- **Opening Book:** Integrate a pre-calculated map of common chess openings (e.g., e4, d4 responses) so the AI moves instantly in the first 5-10 turns without searching.

